Error: case_when() Missing TRUE


Problem


Show the code
bp_clean |&gt; 
  mutate(
    age_cat = case_when(
      age &lt; 40 ~ "Young",
      age &gt;= 60 ~ "Senior"
    )
  ) |&gt; 
  select(age, age_cat)


#&gt; # A tibble: 200 × 2
#&gt;      age age_cat
#&gt;    &lt;dbl&gt; &lt;chr&gt;  
#&gt;  1    36 Young  
#&gt;  2    79 Senior 
#&gt;  3    19 Young  
#&gt;  4    70 Senior 
#&gt;  5    61 Senior 
#&gt;  6    43 &lt;NA&gt;   
#&gt;  7    49 &lt;NA&gt;   
#&gt;  8    23 Young  
#&gt;  9    49 &lt;NA&gt;   
#&gt; 10    72 Senior 
#&gt; # ℹ 190 more rows



Solution


Show the code
bp_clean |&gt; 
  mutate(
    age_cat = case_when(
      age &lt; 40 ~ "Young",
      age &gt;= 60 ~ "Senior",
      TRUE ~ "Middle"
    )
  )

gtsummary Tables in Quarto
gtsummary integrates naturally with Quarto. Use as_kable_extra() or the default print() method for HTML output; use as_gt() for PDF.



Table 1: Baseline characteristics by intervention group.


library(gtsummary)

overall_up |&gt;
  select(current_age, sex, tobacco_type, fuel_type, sbp_0m, intervention) |&gt;
  tbl_summary(
    by      = intervention,
    missing = "no"
  ) |&gt;
  add_p() |&gt;
  add_overall() |&gt;
  bold_labels()



Adjusting output by format:

tbl &lt;- overall_up |&gt;
  tbl_summary(by = intervention)

# HTML output
tbl

# For PDF (via gt)
tbl |&gt; as_gt()

# For Word
tbl |&gt; as_flex_table()

Functions and Control Flow

Functions are reusable blocks of code created with function()
Control flow uses if, else, for, while and repeat



Show the code
add &lt;- function(a, b) {
  result &lt;- a + b
  return(result)
}

if (add(2, 3) &gt; 4) {
  print("Yes, it is greater than 4")
}



Functions help organize logic and avoid repetition
Control flow enables conditional decisions and loops
